{
  "_comment": [
    "#1611: each doctor relationship is read as evidence by users/other sessions; absence of proof never means ok.",
    "This stdlib control drives normalized-fact verdicts, not raw-source collection; actual canonical collector and published-shell regressions are in tests/test_cicd_doctor.py. Historical config absence is unknown; the explicit Actions/Woodpecker mismatch is labelled constructed.",
    "The constructed anchor masks only drift as ok, preserving known-good and unknown cases; it misses each of the four relationship drift lines. Fallback facts describe offline plans, never probe execution."
  ],
  "gate": "lib/cicd/doctor.py",
  "invocation": [
    "python3",
    "controls/doctor-ci/run-case.py",
    "{gate}",
    "{case}"
  ],
  "good_exit": 0,
  "good_signal": "^DOCTOR_ROW: ok ",
  "detect_signal": "^DOCTOR_ROW: drift ",
  "unknown_signal": "^DOCTOR_ROW: unknown ",
